<title>DUBAI: UAE lifts ban on Irish beef.</title>
<headline>UAE lifts ban on Irish beef.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates has decided to lift a ban on Irish beef imposed after the &quot;mad cow&quot; scare and announced a ban on the import of foodstuffs and sweets containing beef gelatin of British origin.</p>
<p>Local newspapers said the decisions were taken on Wednesday by the general secretariat of UAE municipalities.</p>
<p>Gulf Arab states maintain a British beef ban, in some cases introduced even before the mad cow disease scare erupted last year.</p>
</text>
